  "review": "See docs/handoff/security-2026-09/client-lifetime.html for input/result categories, uncached operations and local state ownership. Every changed mutation-capable module requires renewed sensitivity review. Self-configuration preparation and rollout review retain only revision, generation, request ID and plan digest metadata; factor codes remain in sensitive local state and factor responses bypass mutation caches. Hashes were re-pinned after merging origin/main: the design-system migration (routes moved onto the shared ui primitives Dialog/Menu/Alert/Button/Select and helpers) and the react/set-state-in-effect refactor (resets moved from effects to useResetOnChange, seeded useState, or key-based remounts) both changed module bytes without adding a mutation surface, cache boundary, or plaintext ownership. Literal NUL bytes accidentally written into signature template literals were replaced with the \\u0000 escape (no runtime change). The sensitivity posture is unchanged.",
